00:28:42.380 --> 00:28:44.397
And we showed you
this briefly before.

00:28:47.320 --> 00:28:52.057
And here we have our errors that
are kind of organized by kind.

00:28:52.057 --> 00:28:53.640
And off to the right,
we have one that

00:28:53.640 --> 00:28:55.280
happened three minutes ago.

00:28:55.280 --> 00:28:57.220
And I think this-- just
going to go on a limb

00:28:57.220 --> 00:28:59.511
and say this is probably the
one that we want to click.

00:28:59.511 --> 00:29:01.580
This probably is
what we saw before.

00:29:01.580 --> 00:29:03.630
It's also telling us
that the status that it's

00:29:03.630 --> 00:29:07.600
seeing for these is 500, which
matches the big sea of red

00:29:07.600 --> 00:29:10.430
that you saw before.

00:29:10.430 --> 00:29:13.530
So we're going to click this.

00:29:13.530 --> 00:29:16.800
And we're looking at
the error details.

00:29:16.800 --> 00:29:20.230
At the top of the page here,
the top table that we've got,

00:29:20.230 --> 00:29:23.430
we see some of the
same information

00:29:23.430 --> 00:29:27.230
that we saw in the Overview page
